        "original_id": "f854f795-9527-504e-971f-07ab2629a6f8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Grandtheft, Aaron Waisglass, Rihanna\n- Roles: DJ, musician, trap artist, singer\n- Places: Toronto, Canada, Barbados\n- Songs: “Summer,” “Sweet Nothing,” “Bitch Better Have My Money”\n- Topics: remixes, digital releases, chart recognition\n\nFacts:\n- Grandtheft is the stage name of Aaron Waisglass, a Canadian DJ and musician based in Toronto.\n- Grandtheft gained recognition as a trap artist for remixing songs including “Summer,” “Sweet Nothing,” and “Bitch Better Have My Money,” and for having songs chart around the world.\n- Rihanna is a Barbadian singer who recorded the song “Bitch Better Have My Money.”\n- “Bitch Better Have My Money” was digitally released through the iTunes Store on March 26, 2015.",
